David,

We all of course play differently. My early to midgame goals are
typically (in order):

1) AC down to about -20 including all protections, armor, and enchantments.

2) Weight management. Sokoban gives a 50/50 chance here as does tool shops
   in Minetown. Sokoban always helps by pumping weight.

3) MR/MC/reflection. Again 50/50 for reflection in Sokoban. MC/MR is catch
   as catch can.

4) Holy water. Convert an altar if it's in the first 10 levels or so. 
   Presuming that MR/MC comes available, then usually I poly the pet
   to level it up, and then let it take on priests and shopkeeps in
   Minetown. After the priest is gone, I then convert the minetown
   altar. Holy water in a Nethack game is like nitrous in an engine.

5) Reliable ID. Use shops early on. Use ID scrolls as you find them
   (bless of course). Use +ID or magic marker when you come across it.

6) Unihorn. Unicorns are really no match for XL9+ pets.

Once I have these I consider myself to officially be in midgame and preparing
for the Quest. An early wish or two is nice but not absolutely required.
If I get an early wish via throne, smoky potion, or magic lamp (the
latter two require holy water and decent luck) then GDSM is the first item
of choice because it significantly impacts each of the first 3 major goals
on the list: it's light, it significantly lowers AC, and confers MR.
Izchak occasionally has magic lamps as do the tool shops.

I learned long ago that AC and weight are the twin killers of early characters.
Bumping XL quickly adds to that because then tougher monsters come faster.

The protection racket significantly impacts my top two goals. I get significantly
lowered AC, and I get it at no weight cost. I get a useful pet as an added bonus.

It's my early game strategy. I do suffer my share of stupid deaths. Traps are
tough in the early game. 

But when I use to just go whacking in the early game, I found that both my pet,
who was weaker, and myself, who was facing stronger monsters earlier, were both
getting waxed by the RNG on the regular.

It my not be for everyone. But it's just my 2 cents.

